  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Application Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m now structuring the application, focusing on the core design. I\'m taking the initial user prompt and translating the top bar elements (phone and email) into the overall layout. This is where I\'m at now, mapping the initial requirements to visual elements.\n\n\n**Mapping Feature Implementation**\n\nI\'ve progressed to mapping specific features to visual elements. The header now includes the logo and search bar. The main menu is structured with all section links, including the \"Catalog\" dropdown. I\'m focusing on the home page, specifically the hero slider and quick category tiles, considering how to showcase these elements effectively.\n\n\n**Structuring Page Content**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the content structure for specific pages. I\'ve broken down the \"About Us\" page, outlining sections for history, achievements, and credentials. Next, I am preparing the catalog page. I\'m focusing on its multi-parameter filter sidebar, including categories, price ranges, brands, availability, and technical specifications, as well as the active filters display.\n\n\n**Detailing Product Display**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the product display features, working through various sorting options like popularity, price (ascending and descending), and rating. I\'m focusing on grid/list view toggles, product card components with high-res images and key details, interactive quick views, and pagination. I\'m prioritizing the inclusion of add-to-cart functionalities, comparison tools, and wish list integration.\n\n\n**Elaborating Product Details**\n\nI am now delving into the product page. I\'ve broken it down to consider detailed technical specifications, downloadable manuals, customer reviews with submission options, and cross-sell recommendations. Moving on to the \"Services\" page, I\'m structuring a comprehensive list of professional audio engineering services, including design, installation, maintenance, and rental, with detailed service cards, estimates, and order options.\n\n\n**Developing Supporting Content**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding supporting content. I\'ve outlined the \"News\" section, which will feature a grid view with summaries and modals or expanded pages for detailed views. I\'ve also planned the \"Articles & Knowledge Base\" with detailed guides. Next, I\'m working on the \"Certificates & Documents\" page, planning a gallery view with high-res zoomable images, and download options for PDFs and other documents.\n\n\n**Adding Final Pages**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final pages, starting with the FAQ section, structured with accordions and a live search. The partner section now features a brand grid and details. The contacts page includes an interactive map, comprehensive requisites, and contact forms. I\'ve begun working on the cart and checkout page with interactive item management and stock verification.\n\n\n**Finalizing Checkout Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final checkout details. Specifically, I\'m focusing on implementing promo code application, total calculation with a VAT toggle, and quick export options for commercial proposals and payment invoices. I\'m also developing the multi-step checkout process with a modular form, starting with customer type selection, contact information and requisites (especially for B2B), delivery method options, payment methods, and finally, order confirmation with order number generation. Finally, I\'m integrating detailed payment and delivery terms, particularly for B2B legal entities, including details on VAT and invoice generation.\n\n\n**Integrating Data & Modules**\n\nI\'m now integrating B2C retail payment options, including \320\225\320\240\320\230\320\237, Cards, and Installment plans. I\'m building a delivery calculator widget and planning for Minsk, regional centers, and rural areas. I\'m focusing on a bonus module with 1C and Excel data integration. I am implementing an interactive modal/drawer simulating 1C enterprise catalog sync and also import from and export to Excel/XML/JSON. I\'m organizing the codebase into modular files for data structures, mock data and the AppContext.\n\n\n**Defining UI Components**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on defining the UI components. I\'m building `/src/components/layout/Header.tsx` for the top bar and main header. `/src/components/layout/Footer.tsx` will include the sitemap and contact details. I\'m also preparing common components like badges, rating stars, modals, and notifications, including components for the home page. I\'m also planning the hero slider, categories grid, product showcase, service section, advantages grid, audio configurator, brand carousel, and callback form.\n\n\n\n**Structuring Page Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on page-specific components within the `/src/components` directory. I\'m building out a `Card.tsx` component with photo hover and zoom capabilities for product display. I\'m also planning the `QuickViewModal.tsx`. I\'m also preparing `ProductDetailPage.tsx` with all the required views, and working on `ServicesPage.tsx` with a request form. Also, I\'ve outlined `AboutPage.tsx` and the supporting pages.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 17
      nanos: 262481715
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
